  "exact_interfaces": [
    {
      "contract": "_prepare_source_v1(app, exact worker, original job, start_monotonic=original) issues one source session, owner, backend, borrowed capture and sole executor; creates/read-backs preregistration before any initialize/RESET/step/CAPTURE; _check_source_v1 rechecks source/session prereg and exact handles.",
      "source": "research/operational_prefix_v1.py:452"
    },
    {
      "contract": "check_active uses real repository job and unique RUNNING attempt/lease/fencing, calls read_visual_worker_lease without caller now. Do not compare changing observed_at/expiry/state hashes to frozen equality: identity/fencing is frozen; fresh lease observations remain live.",
      "source": "research/operational_prefix_v1.py:366; vision/worker_owner.py:131"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Subclass requires concrete MuJoCoPhysicsBackend/MuJoCoCaptureSession/SkillExecutor-compatible fixtures with same backend; sole recorder.__enter__ registers exactly one observer after backend.initialize. Enter borrowed capture once; it neither initializes nor resets/shuts backend.",
      "source": "vision/raw_recorder_v3.py:110,187; simulation/mujoco/backend.py:245"
    },
    {
      "contract": "BackendOperationBoundary exact fields operation_id/kind/phase/episode_id/physics_step/sim_time_s/parameters/result/error_type/error. Per-ID map supports nested operations. Ledger rows omit sim_time_s/result; D ledger must preserve full detached event snapshots.",
      "source": "simulation/mujoco/backend.py:136,306,358"
    },
    {
      "contract": "owner.begin_event(kind)->exact token; mark_event(token)->None, once; end_event(token)->exact OperationalBracket only after MARK; read_current(after=original capture token)->current bracket; age_bounds(event bracket,current bracket)/within_age(... max_age_ns=5000000000). Token/receipt identity and same domain object required; descriptor equality is diagnostic.",
      "source": "research/operational_time_v1.py:312"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Operational _on_boundary first allocates D attempt then tees super. Preserve legacy _clock_pair tuple (seq,MONOTONIC before,UTC,MONOTONIC after) and separate RESET journal; never relabel these as D. New D tee consumes event snapshot only; legacy super behavior remains unchanged.",
      "source": "research/native_reset_capture_v2.py:77,85"
    },
    {
      "contract": "RESET BEGIN can have null/old episode; RESET END has new episode. Preserve original S_BEGIN/S_END; RESET cached CAPTURE nests under RESET with a separate operation/token. step(120) produces CONTROL+PHYSICS per step and one actual cached-render CAPTURE afterwards; one explicit recorder.capture adds a fresh actual CAPTURE. Normal recipe has three captures, but runtime allocations govern failures/full denominator.",
      "source": "simulation/mujoco/backend.py:518,554,739,1083"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Actual CAPTURE allocation/acquisition identity comes from inherited _allocated_frames/_operations; link D token/bracket to that acquisition, including failed allocation with no completed frame. Pure cache read/derived input retains original source_acquisition_id and source bracket; cannot refresh image age from read timestamp.",
      "source": "vision/raw_recorder_v3.py:491,565,609"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Backend swallows BaseException from observers and retains operation_observer_failures. Successful function return is insufficient: runner checks backend failure ledger, D partials, super _audit_failures, missing/duplicate/foreign boundaries. Error END, missing END or result reconstruction failure produce archived incomplete rows; do not synthesize MARK/END.",
      "source": "simulation/mujoco/backend.py:343; research/native_reset_capture_v2.py:122"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Publication uses original repository.publication_guard; recheck live source/handles/config/asset/lease/fencing and original-reader verdict inside guard; persist new receipt/catalog exclusively before exposing private live catalog. Failed write/export yields no live catalog, preserves original failure; late finally/export errors cannot replace original exception.",
      "source": "research/native_clock_publication_v2.py:737; simulation_runtime/sqlite_repository.py:53"
    },
    {
      "contract": "Inherited legacy exporter/_save_frames/flush are writable and may run again on __exit__; new layer must account for repeated saves, preserve exact frozen legacy payload and original frame bytes, export failure ledger and acquisition allocation census. Avoid treating legacy export's INCOMPLETE default as new source verdict.",
      "source": "research/native_reset_capture_v2.py:154; vision/raw_recorder_v3.py:840,929,937"
    },
    {
      "contract": "R03 public reader hardcodes explicit_acquisitions==0, so its verdict cannot be reused for OC2 explicit1. Worker generic terminal selection currently understands only NATIVE_RESET_PREFIX_EXCLUDED and VISION_CLOSED_LOOP special cases; do not expand _execute beyond allowed early branch. New incomplete source needs existing failure path or another within-scope resolution; any need to change terminal mapper requires Astra.",
      "source": "research/native_clock_publication_v2.py:647; simulation_runtime/worker.py:213"
    }
